WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.108
A deployment script should be predictable
and easy to review.

2
00:00:06.188 --> 00:00:13.845
Avoid building one large command string
from variable data and then asking the shell

3
00:00:13.925 --> 00:00:15.974
to interpret it again.

4
00:00:16.054 --> 00:00:22.956
Keep the command structure fixed, quote
values that should remain literal,

5
00:00:23.036 --> 00:00:29.291
and use arrays for options and operands
where that improves clarity.

6
00:00:29.371 --> 00:00:32.929
The less a script relies on re-parsing,

7
00:00:33.009 --> 00:00:37.862
the easier it is to understand what will
actually run.

8
00:00:37.942 --> 00:00:43.334
Inputs to deployment tools should be
validated before use.

9
00:00:43.414 --> 00:00:50.532
Namespaces, resource names, labels, file
paths, chart names, release names,

10
00:00:50.612 --> 00:00:53.847
image references, timeout values,

11
00:00:53.927 --> 00:00:59.212
and environment names all influence what
the script does.

12
00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:04.252
Validation does not need to be elaborate
in every case,

13
00:01:04.332 --> 00:01:11.234
but the script should reject unsupported
or empty values before they shape a

14
00:01:11.314 --> 00:01:13.256
deployment command.

15
00:01:13.336 --> 00:01:19.590
Working directory control matters because
manifests, Helm charts,

16
00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:26.357
Kustomize overlays, and generated files
often depend on relative paths.

17
00:01:26.437 --> 00:01:33.231
A script should not silently change
behavior because it was launched from a

18
00:01:33.311 --> 00:01:37.193
different directory or runner workspace.

19
00:01:37.273 --> 00:01:39.753
Tool versions also matter.

20
00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:47.167
kubectl, Helm, Kustomize, and supporting
tools may produce different output or

21
00:01:47.247 --> 00:01:51.453
enforce different behavior across
versions,

22
00:01:51.533 --> 00:01:58.003
so important workflows should document or
control expected versions.

23
00:01:58.083 --> 00:02:02.828
Exit status and result handling should be
explicit.

24
00:02:02.908 --> 00:02:10.781
A script should distinguish expected
no-change results from failures and stop before

25
00:02:10.861 --> 00:02:14.959
later steps trust an incomplete
deployment.

26
00:02:15.039 --> 00:02:20.323
If a render step fails, the apply step
should not continue.

27
00:02:20.403 --> 00:02:26.335
If an apply step fails, a rollout check
should not report success.

28
00:02:26.415 --> 00:02:33.640
Clear, non-sensitive errors help operators
respond without exposing tokens,

29
00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:39.220
kubeconfig contents, secrets, or sensitive
manifest data.
